Z||000007||newfie||10-28-2001||07:56 PM||||I'm thinking about doing the same thing after the winter.  Driving a car from the southern states back here to Newfoundland canada.  What things have to be considered in terms of registration, taxes, duties, insurance that kind of stuff?  I asked this to a few people but can't get a definate answer.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||jelly2m8||10-29-2001||08:56 PM|||| OK guys I'm ready to go, and I'm leaving in a few hours.<P> I'll try and keep an update on where I am, whats goin on.<P> I plan on being at Skitime's over the weekend, and make it to the MAFOA meeting if everything goes as planned.<P> Kempo, I'm gonna give u a call through the week, I might be looking for a place to crash friday nite if that offer is still open.<BR> <BR> I have all the replys from you guys that are offering a helping hand if need be. thanks again on that.<P> Newfie, I'll post on importing a car into canada when I get back, keep reminding me so I don't forget. <BR> Give Canada Customs a call, they will give you the toll free number for the registrar of imported motor vehicles. They will send you packet containing all the information you will need to import a car from the US.<P> K, thats it for now, gotta catch a few ZZZ's before I head to the airport.||||reg||1
