Z||000017||jelly2m8||11-04-2001||09:52 PM||||Just returned home about 7 PM this evening, I'll post soon on my trials and tribulations.....<P> time for some sleep!||||reg||1
Z||000018||jelly2m8||11-08-2001||06:05 PM||||I had a call from a customer wondering what happened with my trip to FL.<P> I thought I would share my experiance.<P> Sorry this is going to be a bit long.<P> First of all I bought a white 88 T-Top coupe off of E-bay for $300.00. <P> The first plan was for me and a buddy  mine to tow it back to Canada, but he backed out at almost the last minute.<BR> I decided on flying down and hopefully driving the car back, as I was told that the car ran well, and was definetly drivable.<P> On Tuesday the 30th of October I flew into Orlando airport in the afternoon. I proceeded in taking a cab to the sellers location. Apon arrival I seen that the car was in rougher condition than the pictures showed. Someone previously painted several of the body panels with a spray bomb, and the interior is pretty much ragged. No big deal, I was only after the chassis and T-tops anyhow.<P> After buying a battery for it at a local autozone, the car would not stay idling, and died when trying to give it throttle. I noticed that the injector spray was weak. Another quick trip to the parts place and a fuel filter and TPS sensor later, still no dice.<P> At this point it was about 9 pm. The fact that I was on the go from 4 am and that the guy that owned it being a total dick, I decided to grab a motel room for the night and make some decisions. <BR> The guy kept going off that the car ran great, and it just needed to be run longer. He was on my last nerve and I said that obviously it doesn't and that I would have it removed first thing in the morning even if I had to tow it. Then he has the nerve and says that I couldn't remove the car untill the evening when him or his wife returned home. What gives, they have my money, I have a reciet...?<P> The next morning bright and early I rented a U-haul and a tow dolly and had that car out of there LONG before they returned home.<BR> I towed the car to Vero Beach where a good friend known as Devotshka on PFF took me in and made me feel at home for several days. <P> We looked the car over, and decided there was numerous things that needed fixing before a drive of such length. Then we threw in the unknown factor ( what else will break over 2000 miles?) and decided that the best bet was to tow it home.<P> Other than keeping the motor running, the car would have needed 4 tires, a balljoint, alignment, wiper blades. The gas guage didnt work, neither did the radio or the right headlight motor.<P> At this point I chilled at devotshka's place, and on Friday morning I rented a Ryder truck and a flat deck. We loaded the car on and my gear in the truck, and away I went.<P> I kinda left there in a big hurry as I was questioning my ability to drive that far alone in 2 days. I have a back problem, and I can't drive more than an hour or so before I have to stop driving. Also I have a habit of getting drowsy on a long drive and have to watch myself closely.<BR> I kept myself alert and as comfortable as possible by changing the temperature and radio station randomly.<P> I made a good 800 plus miles that first day, which was roughly the half distance point I needed to drive before I was able to meet up with my fiancee who brought a truck to Bangor Maine, where we transfered the tow.<BR> I slept about 5 hours somewhere at a rest stop in the northern part of NC.<P> 5am saturday morning I headed out again on what I knew was going to be a long day, travelling the I-95 north through Washington, Philadelphia, NYC, etc. Surprisengly the worst traffic was in CT, and RI.<BR> At almost exactly midnight saturday I hauled into the hotel in Bangor where I met up with Lori my fiancee. After a nice long shower, and a good nights sleep we headed out sunday morning and arrived home that evening. I could'nt believe it, I had done the drive alone!<P> I had planned on stopping and visiting with several members who was willing to lend a helping hand if need be, and to make it to the MAFOA meet in MD on saturday.<BR> I wasn't able to meet these plans as I had to be home before monday morning for other reasons.<BR> Thanks to those of you who offered, and I am really sorry I didn't get chance to stop.<P> On the upside a buddy and me got the car running on monday morning, and I have been driving it all week. The little bugger works great, and I'm really starting to enjoy the merits of the 88 suspension.<P> We checked the fuel pressure first off, and found less than 5 psi. Even though the pump was running we dropped the tank to swap it out. What I found was the rubber hose that connects the pump to the sending unit had rotted, and had a hole in it. I replaced that hose, and it runs nice.<P> While underneath we found that the car is near immaculate under there. looks like a car from up here that is only a year old or so. Very nice!<P> All in all I'm happy with the final cost of the car and getting it home. I have a great base to start with to build my loaded 88 GT.<P> Many thanks go out to those who offered help along the way, and a very special thankyou to Devotshka, you really helped me keep things into view bud! next time I'm staying at you place a lot longer!<BR> <BR> Thats my story, next time if I buy a car from far away, I'll plan on towing it from the get-go. I would do this adventure again in a heartbeat!<P> Oh, BTW customs didn't look or even ask any questions towing that car across the border!<P> So much for the theory on importing it into the country...<P>jelly2m8<BR>  <p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 11-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||Devotshka||11-09-2001||12:58 AM||||No problem, bud.  You're always welcome here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Seeya in IRC!||||reg||10
Z||000020||Back On Holiday||11-10-2001||07:41 AM||||my question for you, did you get the title for the car?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000021||jelly2m8||11-10-2001||08:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Back On Holiday:<BR><B>my question for you, did you get the title for the car?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No I didn't, Apparently the car is the product of a messy divorce. The people I bought it from think that the woman they got it from has found the title for it.<P> In the mean time I have put in a request with the DMV to get it titled.<P> If nothing happens with either of these, I will use the VINS and title off my 87 that I am using to build on this 88 chassis.||||reg||1
